# Production build values. Vite loads this on top of .env when it builds, so
# whatever .env holds for local development cannot reach a deployed bundle.
#
# Both must stay EMPTY / relative. The app then calls /api, /ws and /analytics
# on its own origin and nginx forwards them, which is what web/Dockerfile has
# always done with ENV VITE_API_URL=.
#
# This file exists because a local `npm run build` picked up
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:7060 from .env and shipped it. Every API call,
# login included, then pointed at the *viewer's* own machine and failed with
# net::ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED, while the server logs stayed empty because the
# request never left the browser. The same mistake in the other variable made
# face verification report the analytics service unreachable while it was
# healthy.
VITE_API_URL=
VITE_ANALYTICS_URL=/analytics
